---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
const release = 'v0.1.0'
const base = `https://github.com/jd4rider/nova/releases/download/${release}`
---
<SiteLayout title="Releases" path="releases" description="Nova v0.1.0 preview installers, VS Code extension, checksums, signing status and release policy.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Preview · v0.1.0 · November 2026</span>
      <h1>First public build.</h1>
      <p>Unsigned Nova Studio installers, a standalone macOS CLI archive and the Nova Language VS Code extension, built from this repository. Read the signing warning before launching.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions" style="margin-top: 24px;">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}/Nova-Studio-0.1.0-arm64.dmg`} rel="noreferrer">macOS DMG ↓</a>
        <a class="button" href={`${base}/Nova-Studio-0.1.0-x64-setup.exe`} rel="noreferrer">Windows EXE ↓</a>
        <a class="button" href={`${base}/SHA256SUMS`} rel="noreferrer">SHA-256 sums ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 20px;">
    <div class="wrap grid-2" style="align-items: start;">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Assets</h2>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Asset</th><th>Platform</th><th>Size</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><a href={`${base}/Nova-Studio-0.1.0-arm64.dmg`}>Nova-Studio-0.1.0-arm64.dmg</a></td><td>macOS arm64</td><td>114 MB</td></tr>
            <tr><td><a href={`${base}/Nova-Studio-0.1.0-x64-setup.exe`}>Nova-Studio-0.1.0-x64-setup.exe</a></td><td>Windows x64</td><td>94 MB</td></tr>
            <tr><td><a href={`${base}/nova-0.1.0-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz`}>nova CLI archive</a></td><td>macOS arm64</td><td>852 KB</td></tr>
            <tr><td><a href={`${base}/nova-language-0.1.0.vsix`}>nova-language-0.1.0.vsix</a></td><td>VS Code 1.85+</td><td>309 KB</td></tr>
            <tr><td><a href={`${base}/Nova-Studio-0.1.0-arm64.zip`}>Nova-Studio ZIP</a></td><td>macOS arm64</td><td>110 MB</td></tr>
            <tr><td><a href={`${base}/nova-0.1.0-source.tar.gz`}>Source archive</a></td><td>Source</td><td>Tagged tree</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="notice danger"><strong>Not signed.</strong> macOS: unsigned/not notarized; use right-click → Open or clear quarantine. Windows: unsigned; SmartScreen may warn. The VSIX is an unsigned local extension package and is not Marketplace-published. There are no update signatures or provenance attestations yet.</p>

        <h2>Install everything with Homebrew</h2>
        <p>The Studio cask depends on the language formula, so both are installed in one operation:</p>
        <pre><code>brew install --cask jd4rider/tap/nova-studio
nova --version</code></pre>

        <h2>Release policy</h2>
        <p>Version numbers are tied to a Git tag and emitted artifacts. The build must include the real compiler, Studio and website checks. Future releases should add Developer ID signing, notarization, Authenticode, SBOM/provenance and platform smoke tests.</p>
        <p>See the <a href="https://github.com/jd4rider/nova/blob/main/INSTALL.md">installation guide</a> for direct installs and source builds.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="card">
        <div class="kicker">Compatibility</div>
        <h3>Preview limits</h3>
        <ul class="proof" style="display: grid; gap: 8px;">
          <li>macOS arm64 only for prebuilt Studio/CLI</li>
          <li>Windows Studio cross-built; not launched on Windows</li>
          <li>Windows Studio has no bundled CLI and runs in pipe mode</li>
          <li>No signed/notarized/autoupdate build</li>
          <li>No Intel Mac or Linux installer</li>
          <li>VS Code extension is a local VSIX only</li>
          <li>Extension LSP is full-document sync only</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="meta">Node-pty is omitted from the Windows cross-build because electron-builder cannot cross-compile it from macOS.</div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
